BUG 4 – Search/Filter Does Not Reset Pagination

1. What was the issue?

In App.jsx, the page state was maintained when the user changed
the search query or status filter.
For example, if the user was on Page 3 and then searched for a
term that had only 2 pages of results, the application still
requested Page 3.
This could return an empty result even though matching tasks
existed on Page 1 or Page 2.

2. How did I find it?

I checked the pagination state and the SearchBar and StatusFilter
components in App.jsx.
The page state was initialized with:

const [page, setPage] = useState(1);

But changing the search query or status only updated query/status.
It did not reset the page back to 1.

3. What did I change?
I updated the onChange handlers for both SearchBar and StatusFilter
to reset the page to 1 whenever the search or filter changes.

For example:

onChange={(value) => {
    setQuery(value);
    setPage(1);
}}

4. Why did I change it?

When search criteria change, the available results and number of
pages can also change.
Resetting pagination to Page 1 ensures that the user sees the
matching results instead of an empty page caused by an old page
number.

Result:

Changing the search query or status filter now automatically
starts the results from Page 1.